<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle Friday roundup - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle Friday roundup - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was very slow on Friday, with a few sales slaughter steers and heifers steady, USDA said. Inquiry was fair and demand light.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed on 1,200 slaughter steers and 300 slaughter heifers Friday. Last week's confirmed sales 82,100 head including 31,700 head or about 39 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle. Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink.</p>
<p>Slaughter steers -</p>
<p>Few Select and Choice 2-3 1100-1125 lbs 67.00.</p>
<p>Slaughter heifers -</p>
<p>Few Select and Choice 2-3 1000-1100 lbs 67.00.</p>
<p>Confirmed - 1,500   last week - none   last year - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
